What changed since the previously vendored commit (6715ce6..a88f36f; RTC rework only,
all 2026-10-05):
  a299672  t2smc: read the RTC through the CLKL latch and CLKR rate like AppleSMCRTC
  ef538f9  t2smc: only write CLKO when the RTC offset changed like AppleSMCRTC
  0137d29  t2smc: synchronize CLKO with the system clock before sleep and at shutdown
  3772fcc  rtc-sync: let chrony maintain the SMC RTC with rtcfile and rtcautotrim
  598fe57  rtc-sync: restore the boot-time hwclock sync, chrony rtcfile needs RTC interrupts
  Also: T2SMC_VERSION 0.0.1 -> 0.0.2, new CLKL/CLKR keys, new suspend/shutdown PM
  ops, README and tools/t2smc-rtc-client.c additions. No fan or charge-limit changes.
  Log: https://github.com/kaiT2en/KaiT2en-Fedora/compare/6715ce6...a88f36f

Upstream services (not shipped here):
  scripts/fedora/install-rtc-sync.sh is a Fedora-only installer that writes a
  systemd unit running `chronyc waitsync 180 && hwclock --systohc --utc` against
  the t2smc RTC. It is not part of the DKMS module and is not installed by our
  image.

